course: dictionary
lesson: 3603
title: Fiftieth: position and fraction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fiftieth tells you the position in a row or order, like first, second and third. In «He loses the soap for the fiftieth time», it means the 50th time, so he has lost it again and again.
explain: Fiftieth can also be a fraction. One fiftieth means one of fifty equal parts, written 1/50. If a cake is cut into 50 equal slices, one slice is one fiftieth of the cake.
explain: To check the meaning, swap in 50th. «He loses the soap for the 50th time» still makes sense, and the sentence is about the dog losing soap over and over, which fits a big number. When you see fiftieth in maths, ask whether it means a position or a fraction.
fact: Fiftieth is the ordinal of fifty, written 50th.
fact: «Fiftieth» means coming as number 50 in a row or order.
fact: One fiftieth means one of fifty equal parts, written 1/50.
fact: One fiftieth is 0.02, which is 2%.
fact: Fiftieth is used for special days, such as «Grandpa's fiftieth» birthday or a fiftieth anniversary.
exercise: «He loses the soap for the fiftieth time.» Which number does fiftieth stand for? | 500 | *50 | 15 | 5
exercise: What is one fiftieth written as a fraction? | *1/50 | 50/1 | 1/500 | 1/5
exercise: Which birthday is Grandpa's fiftieth? | His 5th | *His 50th | His 15th | His 500th
test: If a pizza is cut into 50 equal slices, what is one slice? | *One fiftieth of the pizza | Half the pizza | Fifty pizzas | One fifth of the pizza
test: What is one fiftieth as a percentage? | *2% | 5% | 20% | 0.2%
exam: Which sentence uses fiftieth to mean a position in a row? | She ate a fiftieth of the cake. | She has fifty pounds in her purse. | She counted to five. | *She finished the race in fiftieth place.
